From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:25:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gpu compositor: the band frames composed on the CPU from the
 tiles (T-505 item 4, a switch)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

JIHAD_GPU_CPU_BANDS=1: a band frame (a scroll-only frame, or one whose change fits the band pass; full-width
bands, no column chunks, not a verify frame) whose band rows are covered by tiled painted layers and colour
layers alone — each "over" at full opacity, no mask, under no container composed apart, with a 2D effective
transform of scale 1 and a translation of whole pixels, every tile under the bands a shared-memory buffer of
B8G8R8A8/X8 whose read lock the host holds — is composed by the compositor thread copying the tiles' pixels
(and filling the colour layers) into the slot's band rows after the kept rows are shifted: no GL composite, no
glReadPixels, no upload for those tiles. The tree is prepared as a composite prepares it (the shadow properties,
the async transforms at this frame's scroll, the parts hidden for a frame without them, the diff taken and
dropped so its baseline is this frame's) and the composite's bookkeeping follows (the scheduler's compose time,
the next frame asked for an animation or a composite-until time, DidComposite). Anything else under a band sends
the frame to the GPU band pass as before; the reasons are counted ("cpu bands:" every 20 band frames) and the
CPU frames timed ("compositor thread: cpu band frame"). Under the switch BufferTextureHost::MaybeUpload keeps a
tile's read lock after its immediate upload, so the content side double-buffers the tile instead of painting its
next content into the buffer the compositor thread copies. TiledContentHost exposes its buffers (JihadTiles,
JihadLowResTiles). The census of 0074 is replaced by the switch's own count.

The review's fixes are in (docs/rounds/finger-2026-11-04/notes.txt, context/impl/impl-review-findings-t505-cpubands.md
in Jihad-Browser): the read lock kept, intermediate surfaces refused, the clear white as the window target's, the
animations' clock noted, the tolerances at float noise, MayResample read from the layer, the band clip before the
tiles are touched, image and canvas layers refused, the composite-until renewal. Off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
